From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vinicius Deolindo <viniciusd@metalbear.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:31:43 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] SlimDetours: include sdkddkver.h with the Windows SDK's casing

SlimDetours.inl included `SdkDdkVer.h`, but the Windows SDK names the
file `sdkddkver.h`. Windows file systems ignore case, so builds on
Windows found it. Builds for MSVC on Linux and macOS read the SDK from
a case-sensitive file system, so the build script failed with:

    fatal error: 'SdkDdkVer.h' file not found

The include now uses the SDK's own name, which every file system finds.
---
 vendor/minhook-detours/SlimDetours/SlimDetours.inl |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/vendor/minhook-detours/SlimDetours/SlimDetours.inl b/vendor/minhook-detours/SlimDetours/SlimDetours.inl
--- a/vendor/minhook-detours/SlimDetours/SlimDetours.inl
+++ b/vendor/minhook-detours/SlimDetours/SlimDetours.inl
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 ﻿#pragma once
 
-#include <SdkDdkVer.h>
+#include <sdkddkver.h>
 
 #include "SlimDetours.NDK.inl"
 #include "SlimDetours.h"
